<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Describing a stretch</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Triangle PQR, with \(P({@P0[1]@},\,{@P0[2]@})\), \(Q({@Q0[1]@},\,{@Q0[2]@})\) and \(R({@R0[1]@},\,{@R0[2]@})\), is mapped onto triangle \(P'Q'R'\), with \(P'({@P1[1]@},\,{@P1[2]@})\), \(Q'({@Q1[1]@},\,{@Q1[2]@})\) and \(R'({@R1[1]@},\,{@R1[2]@})\), by a stretch.</p><p>(a) Which axis is invariant?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The stretch factor is</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) The matrix of the stretch is</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Every [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-coordinate stays the same and every [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]y[[else]]x[[/if]]-coordinate changes, so the points move parallel to the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]y[[else]]x[[/if]]-axis, at right angles to the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis. The [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis is invariant.</p><p>(b) Stretch factor = new distance from the invariant axis \(\div\) old distance. For P: \({@abs(if ax="x" then P1[2] else P1[1])@} \div {@abs(if ax="x" then P0[2] else P0[1])@} = {@k@}\).</p><p>(c) The images of (1, 0) and (0, 1) are the columns: \({@ta@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
/* Design: describe a stretch. Source: original. No vertex lies on either axis, so every vertex moves; k, 1/k and k - 1 are distinct on every entry. Option "neither axis" is first and never correct. */
slist: [["y",2,[[-2,-1],[4,2],[2,-3]]],["x",5/2,[[-1,-1],[-3,-4],[1,-3]]],["y",1/2,[[-4,-3],[4,-3],[-3,3]]],["x",4,[[4,-2],[-2,-1],[-4,-2]]],["y",3/2,[[-1,-3],[-3,-4],[2,1]]],["x",6,[[1,1],[-3,-1],[-2,-2]]],["y",1/4,[[1,-2],[3,2],[2,-1]]],["x",7/2,[[-3,4],[-2,3],[-4,-1]]],["y",3/4,[[4,2],[3,4],[-3,-4]]],["x",2/5,[[1,2],[-3,-2],[4,-2]]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
ax: slist[ix][1]; k: slist[ix][2]; V: slist[ix][3];
ta: if ax="x" then matrix([1,0],[0,k]) else matrix([k,0],[0,1]);
ma(a,f) := if a="x" then matrix([1,0],[0,f]) else if a="y" then matrix([f,0],[0,1]) else matrix([nostretch,0],[0,0]);
imv(v) := list_matrix_entries(ta.transpose(matrix(v)));
P0: V[1]; Q0: V[2]; R0: V[3]; P1: imv(P0); Q1: imv(Q0); R1: imv(R0);
opt1: [["neither",false,"neither axis"],["x",is(ax="x"),"the x-axis"],["y",is(ax="y"),"the y-axis"]];
oax: if ax="x" then "y" else "x";
/* diagnostics: (b) 1/k (object over image), k - 1 (moved over distance); (c) the other axis's matrix; follow-through */
ik: 1/k; km: k-1; dW: ma(oax,k); dWr: ma(oax,1/k);
tw: ta+matrix([0,1],[0,0]); kw: k+1;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
